==============================================================================
4. KILL CRITERION — the placebo
==============================================================================
  Each season's line is slid by a fixed number of days and everything is
  refitted. A real line must stand out from its neighbours. In the parent
  spike three shifted dates were individually MORE significant than the
  true line, and the pedigree cut gets no easier test.

  top-100, observed-deep
    true line   GLM 0.529 (p=0.577, LRT p=0.556)   exact 0.333 (p=0.400) on 5
    placebo shifts at least as large: 20 of 25  ->  permutation p = 0.808
    placebo shifts individually significant at p<0.05: 0

  top-30, observed
    true line   GLM 1.413 (p=0.679, LRT p=0.678)   exact 1.167 (p=1.000) on 7
    placebo shifts at least as large: 8 of 25  ->  permutation p = 0.346
    placebo shifts individually significant at p<0.05: 0

  top-30, all seasons
    true line   GLM 0.757 (p=0.704, LRT p=0.703)   exact 0.859 (p=1.000) on 9
    placebo shifts at least as large: 17 of 25  ->  permutation p = 0.692
    placebo shifts individually significant at p<0.05: 0

  top-100 x line INTERACTION under the same placebo sweep
    true line 1.250 (p=0.505)
    placebo shifts at least as large: 10 of 25  ->  permutation p = 0.423
    placebo shifts individually significant: 4 (shifts 8, 10, 12, 14)

==============================================================================
5. KILL CRITERION — roster need
==============================================================================
  Injured-list placements by the promoting club in the 21 days before the
  promotion, at the arriving man's own side of the roster. In the parent
  spike this ran AGAINST the clock reading: need is higher BEFORE the line.

  top-100, observed-deep       before the line 2.38 (n=13)   after 1.53 (n=57)
  top-30, observed             before the line 1.83 (n=6)   after 1.36 (n=28)
  the whole cohort, for scale  before the line 2.26 (n=155)   after 1.64 (n=679)

==============================================================================
6. KILL CRITERION — club fixed effects
==============================================================================
  The parent spike showed a club dummy is ORTHOGONAL to the line: the line
  falls on the same date for all thirty clubs in a season, so adding club
  dummies cannot move the coefficient, and its doing nothing is arithmetic
  rather than a passed test. That reasoning is unchanged here, so it is not
  repeated as though it were evidence.

  The within-club question the parent asked instead — give every club its
  own line coefficient and test whether they differ — CANNOT be asked at
  this grain, and the reason is countable:
    top-100, observed-deep       70 promotions across 27 clubs — 2.59 per club
    top-30, observed             34 promotions across 24 clubs — 1.42 per club
    top-10, observed             12 promotions across 10 clubs — 1.20 per club
  A model asking thirty clubs to differ needs thirty coefficients. It is not
  run, and no club is named.

