9. What the raw calendar looks like, before any control
==============================================================================
  This is the number the day-of-season shape explains away in the parent
  spike. It is shown for completeness, not as evidence.

  top-100, observed-deep       57 of 70 promotions fall after the line (81.4%)
  top-30, observed             28 of 34 promotions fall after the line (82.4%)
  top-10, observed             10 of 12 promotions fall after the line (83.3%)
  the whole cohort, for scale  679 of 834 promotions fall after the line (81.4%)

  Every grain sits near the cohort share, and the cohort share is mostly
  exposure: only a week or two of the first forty-five days sits before the
  line at all.

